4. Bibliographic Reference Data (Grand Comics Database Attribution)
========================================================================

Galactic Library incorporates bibliographic issue boundary and numbering
data in src/lib/publication-reference-data.js to support comic publication
resolution and coverage analysis (documented in
docs/architecture/publication-resolution.md).

Source Attribution and License:
Reference publication boundaries, numbering sequences, and issue counts
were verified against and derived in part from public bibliographic records
hosted by the Grand Comics Database (GCD, https://www.comics.org).

The Grand Comics Database makes its content available under the Creative
Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC-BY-SA 4.0),
available at: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Derived Data and Modifications:
The bibliographic reference data in src/lib/publication-reference-data.js
reflects specific comic publication runs, including:
- IDW Publishing Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles (ongoing runs, miniseries,
  micro-series installments, macro-series installments, and one-shots).
- DC Comics Elseworlds and related standalone one-shot publications.
- Marvel and Mirage/Image reference entries.

These records have undergone transcription, normalization, and adaptation
for automated collection matching:
- Verification of historical publication dates against collected reprint collections.
- Normalization of issue numbers and standardization of finite issue arrays.
- Grouping of individual micro-series and macro-series installments under parent
  continuities.
- Selection and mapping of publisher and title aliases to match varying metadata
  conventions encountered across local user library records.

Copyright Separation:
Under applicable copyright law, purely factual historical publication data
(such as issue numbers, publication dates, and issue counts) constitutes
uncopyrightable factual information. To the extent that any selection,
coordination, or arrangement of this reference data constitutes protectable
database content or creative expression, it is attributed to the Grand Comics
Database under the CC-BY-SA 4.0 license.

The software code, algorithms, matching heuristics, and validation logic in
Galactic Library are original works licensed under the GNU General Public
License version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later). While Creative Commons
recognizes CC-BY-SA 4.0 as one-way compatible for adaptations into GPLv3
software, this does not imply that CC-BY-SA material is automatically licensed
under every future GPL version, nor does it convert third-party CC-BY-SA
reference data into GPL-licensed code. The underlying factual reference data
remains attributed under CC-BY-SA 4.0 and is not claimed as original GPL-licensed
software.

